# Better Chat Cut

- Project name: **Better Chat Cut** (technical: `better-chat-cut`).
- This is a personal fork of OpenChatCut. Keep LICENSE and upstream attribution.
- Prefer new code under `extensions/`, `packages/`, `docs/`, and `.cursor/` over editing OpenChatCut core.
- Do not refactor upstream code without a clear need. Do not reformat whole upstream files.
- Do not create extra long-lived branches; develop on `main`.
- Never `git push --force`. Never `git reset --hard` on `main`.
- Do not auto-run `/sync-openchatcut`; only when the user explicitly invokes it.
- Future components must be reusable across projects and themes.
- Future assets need manifest, ID, version, category, tag, and capability metadata.
- Agents must search/reuse catalog assets before creating new ones.
- Do not embed one-off generated component source into projects when a catalog asset can be referenced by ID + version.
